{
  "dom_id": "step-q162611",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\n- $F(x,y)=4{y}^{2}x\\,i-x{y}^{2}\\,j$\n- $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y\\,i+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y\\,j$\n- $F(x,y)=2yx\\,i-{y}^{2}\\,j$",
  "worked_solution": "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D\u2286{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $\u03c8(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each vector field.\n\n- Vector field I doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}=4{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y} & =-2xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=4{y}^{2}+(-2xy)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II has a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y,\\,\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y} & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y)=0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III has a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}=2y,\\,\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y} & =-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=2y+(-2y)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
